From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: enable rxlock workaround for the PON PCS

The ETH PCS variant recovers a stuck USXGMII RX (PCS reporting link
down while the RX SigDet module still detects a signal) by triggering a
CDR reset from pcs_get_state(). The PON PCS variant does not use the
workaround, so a stuck RX on a PON PCS port persists until the attached
PHY gives up and retrains the copper link.

The workaround only operates on per-port regmaps and is not specific to
the ETH variant. Enable it for the PON PCS as well.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -1391,6 +1391,7 @@
 	.alloc_regmap_fields = an7581_pcs_alloc_regmap_fields,
 	.bringup = an7581_pcs_bringup,
 	.link_up = an7581_pcs_phya_link_up,
+	.rxlock_workaround = an7581_pcs_rxlock_workaround,
 };
 
 static const struct airoha_pcs_match_data an7581_pcs_pcie = {
